{{also|Gestalt}}
==English==

===Alternative forms===
*[[Gestalt]]

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{etyl|de}} {{term|Gestalt||shape, figure, form}}.  The German term can also apply to a geometric or graphical shape, but that is not the case when this word is used in English.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/gəˈʃtælt/|/gəˈʃtɑːlt/}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/gəˈʃtɑlt/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[collection]] of [[physical]], [[biological]], [[psychological]] or [[symbolic]] [[entities]] that creates a [[unified]] [[concept]], [[configuration]] or [[pattern]] which is [[greater]] than the [[sum]] of its [[part]]s (of a [[character]], [[personality]], or [[being]])
#: ''This biography is the first one to consider fully the writer's '''gestalt'''.''

====Derived terms====
* [[gestaltic]]
* [[gestalt psychology]]
* [[Gestalt therapy]]

